full_passage:
Standard Precautions are the minimum infection prevention practices that apply 
to all patient care, regardless of suspected or confirmed infection status of the patient, 
in any setting where healthcare is delivered. These practices are  designed to both 
protect HCPs, and prevent them from spreading infections among patients, especially 
those involving blood-borne pathogens. Standard Precautions include:  
a) hand hygiene; 
b) use of personal protective equipment (e.g. gloves, gowns, masks);  
c) safe injection practices;

• Provide and use appropriately PPE (Personal Protective Equipment)  when potentially 
exposed to blood and body fluids as part of standard precautions; apron/gowns, gloves, 
visor/face shield; 
• Hand hygiene after handling blood or body fluids;  
• Safe handling of sharps, safer techniques, use of needless devices, sharp box.

